From: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 2 Sep 2026 06:20:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] EXPERIMENT: ASoC: h713: drive the speaker from the HP amp

With 0084 a tone is audible but weak, and -- decisively -- completely
indifferent to volume. Line Out Playback Volume 6/31 against 31/31 is
indistinguishable by ear, DAC Playback Volume 20 against 63 likewise, and an A/B
of stereo against mono differential switched mid-tone produced no difference
either. The registers were provably changing: 0x310 read 0x0015E80F at line-out
volume 15 and 0x0015E87F at 31.

Controls that verifiably move the right register bits while having no audible
effect mean the speaker is not on that output. It is on the HEADPHONE
amplifier, and HP_AMP_EN was never set:

  0x324 = 0x80800C44   HP_EN_L and HP_EN_R set, bit 15 HP_AMP_EN CLEAR

Writing the vendor's configuration word mid-tone made it loud immediately:

  0x324 = 0x80808F8C   HP_AMP_EN plus bits 3, 7, 8 and 9

So add an "HP Amp" supply widget that applies that word on power-up and clears
it on power-down, and make LINEOUT depend on it. The whole vendor word is
applied rather than bit 15 alone: the bits were enabled together in the run that
produced sound, and whether HP_AMP_EN suffices by itself has NOT been tested.

This also retires two earlier null results, which were correct data pointing at
a wrong assumption rather than failures: line-out volume was inaudible because
the speaker is not on line-out, and the route made no difference for the same
reason.

UNTESTED as a driver change -- the register write is proven, the DAPM plumbing
of it is not. Watch for the amp being enabled at the right time rather than
permanently: leaving a headphone amplifier powered into an idle DAC is how you
get hiss.

OUT OF SERIES, applies after 0084.

Signed-off-by: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/sound/soc/sunxi/sun4i-codec.c b/sound/soc/sunxi/sun4i-codec.c
--- a/sound/soc/sunxi/sun4i-codec.c
+++ b/sound/soc/sunxi/sun4i-codec.c
@@ -241,6 +241,15 @@
 #define SUN50I_DAC_DAP_CTL			(0xf0)
 
 #define SUN50I_H616_DAC_AC_DAC_REG		(0x310)
+/*
+ * H713 drives its speaker from the HEADPHONE amplifier, not LINEOUT. Measured:
+ * with HP_AMP_EN clear a tone is audible but weak and completely indifferent to
+ * line-out volume -- 6/31 and 31/31 are indistinguishable, as are stereo and
+ * mono differential. Writing the vendor's configuration word here makes it loud.
+ */
+#define SUN50I_H713_HP_REG			(0x324)
+#define SUN50I_H713_HP_CFG_MASK			(0x8fcc)
+#define SUN50I_H713_HP_CFG_VAL			(0x8f8c)
 #define SUN50I_H616_DAC_LEN			(15)
 #define SUN50I_H616_DAC_REN			(14)
 #define SUN50I_H616_LINEOUTL_EN			(13)
@@ -1269,6 +1278,7 @@
 	{ "Line Out Source Playback Route", "Mono Differential", "Left Mixer" },
 	{ "Line Out Source Playback Route", "Mono Differential", "Right Mixer" },
 	{ "LINEOUT", NULL, "Line Out Source Playback Route" },
+	{ "LINEOUT", NULL, "HP Amp" },
 
 	/* ADC Routes */
 	{ "Left ADC", NULL, "ADC Enable" },
@@ -1981,6 +1991,25 @@
  * and the mux itself are shared with H616 unchanged: they live in DAC_AC_DAC_REG
  * (0x310) and the digital DAC_DPC, both of which exist here.
  */
+/*
+ * Apply the vendor's whole HP configuration word, not just HP_AMP_EN. Bit 15 is
+ * the amplifier enable, but bits 3 and 7-9 are set alongside it by the vendor
+ * driver and were enabled together in the run that produced sound -- whether
+ * bit 15 alone suffices has NOT been tested, so do not trim this without
+ * measuring.
+ */
+static int sun50i_h713_codec_hp_amp_event(struct snd_soc_dapm_widget *w,
+					  struct snd_kcontrol *k, int event)
+{
+	struct snd_soc_component *component = snd_soc_dapm_to_component(w->dapm);
+
+	snd_soc_component_update_bits(component, SUN50I_H713_HP_REG,
+				      SUN50I_H713_HP_CFG_MASK,
+				      SND_SOC_DAPM_EVENT_ON(event) ?
+					      SUN50I_H713_HP_CFG_VAL : 0);
+	return 0;
+}
+
 static const struct snd_soc_dapm_widget sun50i_h713_codec_codec_widgets[] = {
 	/* Digital parts of the DACs */
 	SND_SOC_DAPM_SUPPLY("DAC Enable", SUN4I_CODEC_DAC_DPC,
@@ -2000,6 +2029,12 @@
 	/* Line Out path, without H616's ramp controller at 0x31c */
 	SND_SOC_DAPM_MUX("Line Out Source Playback Route",
 			 SND_SOC_NOPM, 0, 0, sun50i_h616_codec_lineout_src),
+
+	/* The speaker hangs off the headphone amplifier on this SoC. */
+	SND_SOC_DAPM_SUPPLY("HP Amp", SND_SOC_NOPM, 0, 0,
+			    sun50i_h713_codec_hp_amp_event,
+			    SND_SOC_DAPM_PRE_PMU | SND_SOC_DAPM_POST_PMD),
+
 	SND_SOC_DAPM_OUTPUT("LINEOUT"),
 };
 
